{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" where the documentation starts\n\nIn robotics and automation, a control loop is a non-terminating loop that regulates the state of a system. Here is one example: a thermostat in a room. When you set the temperature, that's telling the thermostat about your **desired state**. The act"}},"session_id":"ce98ddcf-ef6a-43ed-983e-86339f179dfc","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"455989e2-1117-4944-b737-cbb2b006686e"}
